    "text": "Finn and Liam had a clear plan for running a yard sale. They met early and checked each item before they began. The work took patience, careful reading, and steady teamwork. At first, one small problem slowed them down, but they stopped, talked, and chose a better step. They kept the tools in order, listened to each direction, and helped one another whenever a task felt hard. By noon, they had finished the first part and were ready for more. Rain had covered the main trail, so they waited beside a train and checked the rail. Finn carried mail in a pail, while Liam held a chain, a nail, and a brush for paint. A snail moved across the plain path. They had to explain how water reached the drain and left a stain. They raised the sign, checked each detail, and made sure the box could contain the grain. The rain passed again, and they gained confidence. No one was afraid because the plan was plain and the team did not fail. When the final task was complete, Finn checked the list one more time. Liam put away the supplies and cleaned the work space. They talked about what had gone well and what they would change next time. The day had not been perfect, but the team had solved each problem. They had read the signs, followed the plan, and stayed focused from start to finish. Both friends felt proud because their effort had made the project better.  Before leaving, Finn checked the main trail, the rail, the drain, and each detail. The rain was gone, and the plain plan had helped the team gain success.",
